IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cor-coroners`

-- Coroners Act 2009 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in cor-coroners.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY

`spouse` MEANS `spouse or de facto partner`
`executor` MEANS `executor named in the will`
`LPR` MEANS `legal personal representative immediately before the death`
`sibling` MEANS `brother or sister`
`stranger` MEANS `another relationship`

§§ `s 5 -- relative`

-- Arguments: relationship, adult, someone later qualified as spouse, the person had a first-group adult relative.
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4: an earlier spouse, superseded by a later one, is not the spouse.
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `spouse` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `parent` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `person standing in loco parentis` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `guardian` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `child` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child under 18 is not an adult.
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `child` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(1)(b): a brother or sister only if there is no (a) relative.
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `sibling` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `sibling` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An executor is not a relative.
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a relative` `stranger` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6A -- senior next of kin`

-- Arguments: relationship, adult, later spouse, spouse available, adult child available, child under 18, parent
-- available, adult sibling available, sibling under 18, coroner treats me under s 6A(2).
-- (a) the spouse, whoever else there is.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `spouse` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A superseded spouse is not.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `spouse` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) an adult child when there is no spouse available; not while a spouse is available.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `child` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `child` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A child of 17 never is.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `child` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) a parent when there is no spouse or child.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent where the only child is under 18: whether that child is "available" is not said (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (d) an adult sibling when there is no spouse, child or parent available.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `sibling` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) an executor or the legal personal representative when no one above is available; not with a parent or an adult
-- sibling available; open where the only sibling is under 18 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `LPR` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6A(2): the coroner may treat the legal personal representative as senior next of kin even when a spouse is available.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `LPR` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `LPR` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A guardian or a stranger is never senior next of kin under s 6A.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `guardian` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6 -- reportable death`

#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `a violent or unnatural death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `a sudden death, cause unknown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `under suspicious or unusual circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `not the reasonably expected outcome of a health-related procedure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `not the reasonably expected outcome of a procedure the regulations exclude` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `while a patient in (or temporarily absent from) a declared mental health facility` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `an expected or natural death` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 18, 19, 21-24 -- which coroner`

`today` MEANS `d` 7 11 2026
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`no circumstance` MEANS `none of these circumstances`

-- Arguments: connection, day of death, today, how the person died, certified, circumstance, age, day of report.
-- A workplace death in NSW, violent: any coroner.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` EQUALS `any coroner`
-- Natural death, certified: no jurisdiction under s 21.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `no circumstance` 80 `any day` EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- Natural death, but no doctor's certificate: any coroner (s 21(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 80 `any day` EQUALS `any coroner`
-- No connection with NSW: none (s 18).
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `no connection` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- s 18(2): a NSW resident dying overseas.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the person was ordinarily resident in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` EQUALS `any coroner`
-- s 19: exactly 100 years before today is within (fork F3); the day before is not.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 7 11 1926) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 30 `any day` EQUALS `any coroner`
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 6 11 1926) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 30 `any day` EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- s 23: a death in police custody -- a senior coroner only, even though it is also reportable (s 22(2)).
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `in police or other lawful custody` 30 `any day` EQUALS `only a senior coroner (the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner)`
-- s 23 jurisdiction even for a certified natural death in a correctional centre.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `an inmate in (or temporarily absent from) a detention centre, correctional centre or lock-up` 60 `any day` EQUALS `only a senior coroner (the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner)`
-- s 24(1)(a): a child in care aged 17; at 18 the limb fails (certified natural death: none).
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child in care` 17 `any day` EQUALS `only a senior coroner (the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner)`
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child in care` 18 `any day` EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- s 24(1)(b): report within the 3 years before the death; exactly 3 years before is within; the day before is not.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child about whom a risk-of-harm report was made under the Care Act` 10 (`d` 3 3 2023) EQUALS `only a senior coroner (the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner)`
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child about whom a risk-of-harm report was made under the Care Act` 10 (`d` 2 3 2023) EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- ... and a report about a sibling, made after the death, does not count.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child whose brother or sister was the subject of such a report` 10 (`d` 4 3 2026) EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction`
-- s 24(1)(e): an adult in specialist disability accommodation.
#ASSERT `Which coroner can hold an inquest` `the remains are in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `living in (or temporarily absent from) specialist disability accommodation or an assisted boarding house` 45 `any day` EQUALS `only a senior coroner (the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner)`


-- s 24(2). Arguments: connection, day of death, today, circumstance, age, day of report, my position.
-- A child who died in police custody (s 23): the person with parental responsibility is owed best endeavours.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `in police or other lawful custody` 15 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent without parental responsibility, child in care at 17: owed.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a child in care` 17 `any day` `a parent without parental responsibility` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- At 18 the person is not a child (s 24(3)): the "if" fails.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a child in care` 18 `any day` `a parent without parental responsibility` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A risk-of-harm report exactly 3 years before the death is within (fork F17); the day before is not.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a child about whom a risk-of-harm report was made under the Care Act` 10 (`d` 3 3 2023) `a family member reasonably expected to have an immediate interest in the outcome` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `a child about whom a risk-of-harm report was made under the Care Act` 10 (`d` 2 3 2023) `a family member reasonably expected to have an immediate interest in the outcome` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A child's death with no s 23 or s 24 circumstance: s 24(2) does not arise.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `no circumstance` 10 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A child in specialist disability accommodation (s 24(1)(e)): owed; an adult there: not a child.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `living in (or temporarily absent from) specialist disability accommodation or an assisted boarding house` 12 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `living in (or temporarily absent from) specialist disability accommodation or an assisted boarding house` 45 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone outside the s 24(2) list: the Act does not say (fork F13).
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `in police or other lawful custody` 15 `any day` `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No connection with NSW, or a death more than 100 years ago: no jurisdiction arises.
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `no connection` (`d` 3 3 2026) `today` `in police or other lawful custody` 15 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the senior coroner try to tell me of my right to a lawyer` `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales` (`d` 6 11 1926) `today` `in police or other lawful custody` 15 `any day` `a person with parental responsibility for the child` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 25, 27-29, 87 -- must there be an inquest`

-- Arguments: as above, then homicide, unclear whether died/who/when/where, manner and cause unclear, suspended or
-- continued under s 78, inquiry outside NSW, Minister or State Coroner directed, Supreme Court ordered.
`in NSW` MEANS `the death, or its cause, happened in New South Wales`
`death day` MEANS `d` 3 3 2026

-- A workplace death whose manner and cause are known: not required; the coroner may dispense.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest is not required, and the coroner may dispense with it`
-- Manner and cause not sufficiently disclosed: required (s 27(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- ... unless suspended or continued under s 78.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest is not required, and the coroner may dispense with it`
-- Possible homicide: required (s 27(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- Identity not disclosed: required (s 27(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `a sudden death, cause unknown` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- A death in custody: required (s 27(1)(b)); a child in care alone is not.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `in police or other lawful custody` 30 `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `in NSW` `death day` `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `a child in care` 12 `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest is not required, and the coroner may dispense with it`
-- s 27(2): an inquest held outside NSW removes the s 27 requirement ...
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `the person was ordinarily resident in New South Wales` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest is not required, and the coroner may dispense with it`
-- ... but not a direction under s 28.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `the person was ordinarily resident in New South Wales` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- No jurisdiction: none to require.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `no connection` `death day` `today` `a violent or unnatural death` FALSE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no coroner has jurisdiction to hold one`
-- s 87(2), (3): a Supreme Court order gives jurisdiction and cannot be dispensed with.
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held` `no connection` `death day` `today` `an expected or natural death` TRUE `no circumstance` 40 `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`


-- s 25(3). Arguments: the coroner dispensed, the coroner's opinion on new evidence.
#ASSERT `Can the coroner still hold the inquest it dispensed with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "if" fails: s 25(3) gives no power (fork F14).
#ASSERT `Can the coroner still hold the inquest it dispensed with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No earlier dispensing: s 25(3) does not arise.
#ASSERT `Can the coroner still hold the inquest it dispensed with` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the coroner still hold the inquest it dispensed with` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 26 -- reasons for dispensing`

-- Arguments: dispensed, asked, sufficient interest, written request for the reasons for refusal.
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for dispensing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must give me written reasons for dispensing with the inquest`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for dispensing` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner must give me written reasons for refusing to give reasons`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for dispensing` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner need not give me reasons`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for dispensing` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner need not give me reasons`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for dispensing` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 26 does not arise`

§§ `s 35 -- reporting`

#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 38 -- certificates`

-- Arguments: doctor's s 38(1) opinion, 72 or older, only ground violent or unnatural, age-related accident, relative objected.
-- A fall at 85 attributable to age: the doctor may certify.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... unless a relative objects first.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under 72: may not.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another person caused the accident: may not.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Sudden and unexplained as well: may not.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No s 38(1) opinion: s 38 does not speak.
#ASSERT `May the doctor certify the cause of death` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 54 -- notice`

#ASSERT `Must the coroner tell me when and where the inquest is` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must give me the time and place`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner tell me when and where the inquest is` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must give me the time and place`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner tell me when and where the inquest is` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner may give me the time and place`
#ASSERT `Must the coroner tell me when and where the inquest is` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle it`

§§ `s 56 -- the body`

#ASSERT `Does the coroner's right to the body come first` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the coroner's right to the body come first` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 57 -- leave`

-- Arguments: relative, exceptional circumstances, sufficient interest.
#ASSERT `Will I be given leave to appear` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner must grant me leave to appear or be represented`
#ASSERT `Will I be given leave to appear` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner may refuse me leave: exceptional circumstances`
#ASSERT `Will I be given leave to appear` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner may grant me leave: sufficient interest`
#ASSERT `Will I be given leave to appear` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act gives me no leave on these facts`

§§ `s 60 -- witnesses`

#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for refusing my witness` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for refusing my witness` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the coroner give me reasons for refusing my witness` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 61(7) -- certified evidence`

-- The family's later civil claim against the employer: the employer's certified evidence cannot be used against it.
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` TRUE `a civil proceeding in a NSW court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` TRUE `a criminal proceeding in a NSW court, other than for the falsity of the evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` TRUE `a hearing before a person or body authorised by NSW law, or by consent, to take evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` TRUE `a criminal proceeding for the falsity of that evidence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` TRUE `a proceeding outside NSW` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can certified evidence be used against the witness` FALSE `a civil proceeding in a NSW court` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 65 -- the file`

#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the coroner's file` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the coroner's file` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the coroner's file` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the coroner's file` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the coroner's file` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 75 -- self-inflicted deaths`

-- A brother of any age, with others in the family, is protected (unlike s 5).
#ASSERT `Can a non-publication order protect me` TRUE `sibling` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a non-publication order protect me` TRUE `stranger` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a non-publication order protect me` TRUE `executor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can a non-publication order protect me` FALSE `parent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May a report of the inquest be published` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May a report of the inquest be published` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a report of the inquest be published` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 79 -- resuming`

`charged` MEANS `a person was charged with an indictable offence about the death (s 78(1)(a))`
`opinion` MEANS `the coroner formed the opinion that a known person committed an indictable offence (s 78(1)(b))`
`notice day` MEANS `d` 1 6 2026

-- Arguments: why suspended, someone charged, where the charge stands, AG/DPP advised, State Coroner directed not,
-- notice day, proposed day.
-- Charge pending: no.
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `charged` TRUE `not finally determined` FALSE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Acquitted and discharged, order 14 days after notice: yes; 13 days: no.
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `charged` TRUE `the person was discharged` FALSE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `charged` TRUE `the person was discharged` FALSE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 14 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `charged` TRUE `no further appeal can be made without an extension of time` FALSE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Suspended on opinion, no charge: not until the AG or DPP advises.
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `opinion` FALSE `not finally determined` FALSE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `opinion` FALSE `not finally determined` TRUE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Suspended on opinion, later charged: s 79(3) governs.
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `opinion` TRUE `not finally determined` TRUE FALSE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 79(5A): State Coroner's direction.
#ASSERT `Can the suspended inquest be resumed` `charged` TRUE `the person was discharged` FALSE TRUE `notice day` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 79(2A): 14 days after 1 June is 15 June; after 20 December, 3 January.
#ASSERT `The earliest day the inquest may be ordered resumed` `notice day` EQUALS `d` 15 6 2026
#ASSERT `The earliest day the inquest may be ordered resumed` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 3 1 2027

§§ `s 81 -- findings`

#ASSERT `Will the findings state the manner and cause of death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the findings state the manner and cause of death` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the findings state the manner and cause of death` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 83 -- fresh inquests`

#ASSERT `Can I apply for a fresh inquest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a fresh inquest` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must a fresh inquest be held on my application` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must a fresh inquest be held on my application` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must a fresh inquest be held on my application` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 83(2), (3).
#ASSERT `May a fresh inquest be held because of how the previous one ended` `terminated before its conclusion because it appeared the person did not die` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a fresh inquest be held because of how the previous one ended` `concluded with a finding or verdict that the person did not die, or that it is uncertain whether they died` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a fresh inquest be held because of how the previous one ended` `held into a suspected death, and the person's remains have since been found in New South Wales` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside s 83(2), (3): no ground under those subsections (fork F15).
#ASSERT `May a fresh inquest be held because of how the previous one ended` `ended in another way` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 84, 85 -- the Supreme Court`

#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court order an inquest on my application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court order an inquest on my application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


-- s 87(1): 21 days after the order is made, the day of making not counted (fork F16).
#ASSERT `The last day to serve the order on the State Coroner` (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 22 6 2026
#ASSERT `The last day to serve the order on the State Coroner` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 1 2027
-- Across 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `The last day to serve the order on the State Coroner` (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 7 3 2028
#ASSERT `Was the order served on the State Coroner in time` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the order served on the State Coroner in time` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 22 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the order served on the State Coroner in time` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 23 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 8.1`

#ASSERT `Can the coroner dispense with the post mortem at my family's wish` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner dispense with the post mortem at my family's wish` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the coroner dispense with the post mortem at my family's wish` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can the coroner keep a whole organ after the body is released` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner keep a whole organ after the body is released` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner keep a whole organ after the body is released` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: desirable, where the inquest stands, may be resumed or a fresh one held.
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `no inquest has been held` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `suspended because of an indictable offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `suspended because of an indictable offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `terminated on a finding that the person had not died` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `quashed by the Supreme Court with a fresh inquest ordered` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `not completed for another reason` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` TRUE `completed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the coroner order the body exhumed` FALSE `no inquest has been held` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can I claim against the post mortem doctor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I claim against the post mortem doctor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I claim against the post mortem doctor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 8.2 -- objections`

-- Arguments: senior next of kin, holds authority, authority-giver refused under s 96(5), coroner satisfied I may be
-- charged, about a post mortem.
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `as senior next of kin, by written notice: ss 96 and 97 apply`
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as senior next of kin, by written notice, but the coroner may refuse it because I have been or may be charged`
-- s 96(5) is about post mortems only: an organ objection stands.
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as senior next of kin, by written notice: ss 96 and 97 apply`
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `as the senior next of kin's authorised person, by written notice with a copy of my authority: ss 96 and 97 apply`
-- s 98(3): no authority after a s 96(5) refusal.
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only as another person, under s 99: the 48-hour notice and the Supreme Court route do not apply`
#ASSERT `How can I object to the post mortem` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only as another person, under s 99: the 48-hour notice and the Supreme Court route do not apply`

-- s 97(1): 48 hours, counted from the notice; at 48 in time, at 48.5 not.
#ASSERT `Is my Supreme Court application in time` TRUE 20 EQUALS `in time: the coroner's direction or order is stayed until the Court decides`
#ASSERT `Is my Supreme Court application in time` TRUE 48 EQUALS `in time: the coroner's direction or order is stayed until the Court decides`
#ASSERT `Is my Supreme Court application in time` TRUE 48.5 EQUALS `out of time: the 48 hours after the notice have passed`
#ASSERT `Is my Supreme Court application in time` TRUE 72 EQUALS `out of time: the 48 hours after the notice have passed`
#ASSERT `Is my Supreme Court application in time` FALSE 10 EQUALS `section 97 does not arise: no section 96(3) notice was given to me`

-- Arguments: objected, notice given, hours since notice, hours the notice gives, applied, hours when applied, order.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `nothing in Part 8.2 holds it back: no senior next of kin objected`
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `not yet: the coroner must first decide on my objection and give me written notice`
-- 47 hours after the notice: not yet; 48: yes, if the notice gave 48.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 47 48 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `not yet: the time the notice gives (at least 48 hours after it) has not come`
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 48 48 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `yes`
-- The notice gives 72 hours: at 60, not yet.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 60 72 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `not yet: the time the notice gives (at least 48 hours after it) has not come`
-- A notice giving only 24 hours does not shorten the 48.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 30 24 FALSE 0 `no order yet` EQUALS `not yet: the time the notice gives (at least 48 hours after it) has not come`
-- Applied at 40 hours: stayed, even at 100 hours.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 100 48 TRUE 40 `no order yet` EQUALS `not while my Supreme Court application is pending: it is stayed`
-- Applied at 50 hours: no stay.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 100 48 TRUE 50 `no order yet` EQUALS `yes`
-- The Court's orders.
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 100 48 TRUE 40 `an order that the post mortem not be conducted` EQUALS `no: the Supreme Court ordered that it not be conducted`
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 100 48 TRUE 40 `an order that it be conducted within limitations` EQUALS `yes, but only within the limitations the Supreme Court set`
#ASSERT `Can the post mortem go ahead now` TRUE TRUE 100 48 TRUE 40 `an order confirming the coroner's direction` EQUALS `yes`

§§ `ss 100, 101 -- disposal`

`bury` MEANS `bury or cremate them, or place them in a permanent resting place`
`research` MEANS `hand them over for anatomical or medical research`
`interstate` MEANS `take them out of New South Wales (not cremated remains)`
`ashes interstate` MEANS `take cremated remains out of New South Wales`
`doctor's notice` MEANS `a doctor's notice under s 39 of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act`
`stillbirth notice` MEANS `a doctor's certificate or notice under s 12(3) of that Act (stillborn child)`
`coroner's order` MEANS `a coroner's order under s 101`
`registrar's certificate` MEANS `a Registrar's certificate under s 51 of that Act`

-- Arguments: what, document issued, I have it or was given it, stillborn, regulations authorise.
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `coroner's order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `doctor's notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `registrar's certificate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 100(1) needs the authorisation in hand (or given); s 100(2) only that it was issued.
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `coroner's order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `interstate` `coroner's order` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `research` `doctor's notice` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `no document` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `interstate` `no document` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `no document` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A stillborn child: the s 12(3) certificate counts; a Registrar's certificate does not.
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `stillbirth notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `registrar's certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `bury` `stillbirth notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Cremated remains leaving NSW: outside s 100(2).
#ASSERT `May I bury, cremate or remove the remains` `ashes interstate` `no document` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Maximum penalties`

#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `failing to report a reportable death (s 35(2))`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `failing to report a reportable death (s 35(2))`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `obstructing a person executing a coronial investigation scene order (s 44)`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `obstructing a person executing a coronial investigation scene order (s 44)`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `obstructing a person executing a coronial investigation scene order (s 44)`)'s `fine and imprisonment both` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `failing to comply with a notice to produce (s 53(5))`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `refusing to be sworn, examined, answer or produce (s 62)`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `contravening an order clearing the court or forbidding publication (s 74(3))`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `contravening an order clearing the court or forbidding publication (s 74(3))`)'s `fine and imprisonment both` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `publishing in breach of a self-inflicted-death order or s 75(5) (s 75(7))`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `publishing a disallowed question, warning, objection or submission (s 76)`)'s `months of imprisonment` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `burying or cremating remains without authority (s 100(1))`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `handing over or removing remains without authority (s 100(2))`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `disrespectful behaviour in coronial proceedings (s 103A)`)'s `days of imprisonment` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `disrespectful behaviour in coronial proceedings (s 103A)`)'s `penalty units` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`What is the maximum penalty` `disrespectful behaviour in coronial proceedings (s 103A)`)'s `fine and imprisonment both` EQUALS TRUE
